# Heartbeat

Copy this to .ucode/HEARTBEAT.md in your project (or run `ucode heartbeat --init` to generate a
starter one). `ucode heartbeat [interval]` re-reads this file fresh on every tick, so you can
edit it between runs without restarting — same idea as OpenClaw's HEARTBEAT.md convention, scoped
down to whatever tools `ucode` already exposes (shell, files, git, etc.), with no messaging
platform, email/calendar, or OS-level access bolted on.

Keep instructions concrete, and define what "nothing to report" looks like, so the agent doesn't
manufacture busywork on quiet ticks.

## Checks

- Run `git status` in this repo. If there are uncommitted changes, summarize what's changed.
- Run the test suite. If anything is failing that wasn't failing last time, report it.
- Otherwise, reply "nothing to report".
